infographic sequence-ascending-steps
data
  title Cache-poisoning defences stack in layers
  desc Each layer raises attacker cost; none alone is sufficient
  order asc
  sequences
    - label 16-bit TXID + fixed port
      desc Original DNS: only 65536 guesses to forge a response (Kaminsky, 2008)
    - label Source-port randomisation (RFC 5452)
      desc ~65K ports x ~65K IDs = ~4 billion combinations to brute-force
    - label 0x20 case-mixing
      desc Echoed QNAME capitalisation adds ~30 bits an off-path attacker cannot observe
    - label DNSSEC + encrypted transport
      desc Signed answers fail authentication if forged; DoH/DoT remove off-path injection
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b #14b8a6 #6366f1
